recommendation:
RECOMMENDED SETUP (internal Cloud.ru brand kit; Windows and macOS; team in Russia; Oct 2026 to 2028)

1) RUNTIME AND PACKAGING
- Ship one CEP bundle (e.g. com.cloudru.brandkit) with two panels:
  - an After Effects panel (AEFT) and a Premiere panel (PPRO);
  - HostList [25.0,99.9];
  - CSXS 11/12 runtime with --enable-nodejs --mixed-context.
- Why CEP:
  - AE has no production UXP yet; only a public beta is promised by Nov 2026.
  - Premiere's CEP stays on by default until Dec 2028, and private distribution is outside Marketplace cut-offs.
  - CEP is the only route that installs without Creative Cloud desktop, UPIA or an Adobe login. That is the key property for a team in Russia.
- Keep all business logic in host-agnostic TypeScript modules behind a thin host adapter (ExtendScript now, UXP later): library client, manifest, font checks, logging, insert recipes.
- Schedule the Premiere UXP port for 2027. Premiere UXP is GA since 25.6 and has insertMogrtFromPath; importMGT already works from ExtendScript.
- Evaluate AE UXP when the beta lands. Re-check Adobe's timeline after every MAX.

2) SIGNING AND INSTALLATION
- Sign every build, betas included. Use ZXPSignCmd 4.1.3:
  - Create the certificate once: `ZXPSignCmd -selfSignedCert RU Moscow Cloud.ru "Cloud.ru Video BrandKit" <pwd> brandkit.p12 -validityDays 3650`
  - Sign each build: `ZXPSignCmd -sign build dist/brandkit-X.Y.Z.zxp brandkit.p12 <pwd> -tsa http://timestamp.digicert.com` (fallback TSA: http://timestamp.apple.com/ts01)
  - Verify in CI: `ZXPSignCmd -verify dist/brandkit-X.Y.Z.zxp -certinfo`
- Keep the .p12 and its password in a vault.
- Release builds contain no symlinks, .DS_Store, __MACOSX, ._* or .debug files.
- Ship the ZXP with install.cmd + install.ps1 (Windows; the .cmd calls PowerShell with -ExecutionPolicy Bypass) and install.command (macOS). The scripts:
  - refuse to run while After Effects or Premiere is open;
  - unzip to a temp folder, then atomically replace %APPDATA%\Adobe\CEP\extensions\com.cloudru.brandkit (mac: ~/Library/Application Support/Adobe/CEP/extensions/…);
  - clear stale cep_cache;
  - print the installed version.
  - No admin rights, Creative Cloud desktop or Adobe ID needed.
- UPIA (`UnifiedPluginInstallerAgent.exe /install` / `--install`) or aescripts' installer is a secondary path only where Creative Cloud is signed in.
- PlayerDebugMode and .debug stay on developer machines.
- On macOS, IT/MDM or a documented right-click > Open avoids Gatekeeper prompts. A notarized .pkg needs an Apple Developer ID.

3) TEMPLATE LIBRARY, RELEASED SEPARATELY FROM THE PLUGIN
- Build step: a script turns the cleaned AE sources into library files:
  - MOGRTs via CompItem.exportAsMotionGraphicsTemplate;
  - alpha clips via aerender;
  - ffprobe validation (codec / fps / resolution / no audio);
  - sha256 checksums and previews;
  - ASCII/NFC slugs of 64 characters or fewer; junk files rejected.
- Publish immutable, content-addressed objects to a versioned Cloud.ru Object Storage bucket over HTTPS. Agree the read-only access model with security.
- Layout: channels/stable.json points to manifests/YYYY.MM.DD.json.
- Each manifest item has:
  - id and semver;
  - type (mogrt | aep | ffx | mov | png | wav | epr);
  - Russian title and tags;
  - app;
  - variants {w, h, fps, size, sha256};
  - requiredFonts (PostScript names);
  - minPluginVersion and a deprecated flag.
- Client behaviour (Node https in CEP):
  - check the ETag on panel start and every few hours;
  - download only new or changed objects to a short local cache: %LOCALAPPDATA%\CloudRuBrandKit\lib on Windows (never Roaming), ~/Library/Caches/CloudRuBrandKit on macOS;
  - write *.part, verify sha256, then rename;
  - switch the active manifest atomically and keep the previous one for rollback;
  - fetch heavy ProRes clips only on first use;
  - when offline, use the last good manifest.
- Optionally sign the manifest with Ed25519 (Node crypto), because this channel can deliver .jsx, .ffx and .aep files.
- The same layout may also be read from an SMB path or a Syncthing receive-only folder (a setting in the panel).
- Not recommended as the main channel: Yandex Disk (desktop sync paid since June 2026, lagging macOS client) and CC Libraries (Adobe cloud dependency).
- On insert:
  - copy the asset into a project-local folder 'Cloud.ru BrandKit/<item>@<ver>/' and import from there, so projects stay portable and contain no per-user paths;
  - tag the inserted item with id@version (AE item.comment; Premiere bin or metadata).

4) MEDIA FORMATS
- Text-bearing, editable elements become MOGRTs:
  - Premiere-authored where the design allows (fast);
  - AE-authored only where AE features are needed;
  - holds stretch through Responsive Design – Time.
- Non-editable alpha elements become QuickTime ProRes 4444:
  - Straight alpha;
  - no audio track unless the sound is intended (SFX ship as separate WAVs);
  - per-aspect variants at a 25 fps base, plus other frame rates if needed;
  - short durations: intro / loop / outro.
- Concrete re-renders:
  - replace the three 600-second course overlays (about 10 GB) with intro + seamless loop + outro, or with a stretchable comp/MOGRT;
  - re-render the 9x16 podcast intro (QuickTime Animation, 413 Mbps) as ProRes 4444;
  - re-time the 24 fps transitions to 25 fps.
- Optional 'lite' PNG-in-MOV variant (3–9x smaller in our test) only for long 1080p/1440p loops, and only after a playback test in Pr/AE on both OSes.
- Not used: QuickTime Animation, CineForm, HEVC-alpha, VP9/WebM, DNxHR-alpha, PNG sequences.

5) FONTS
- IT installs SB Sans 'for all users' on Windows and to /Library/Fonts on macOS, on licensed machines only.
- Font files never go into the ZXP, the library, MOGRTs or collected projects.
- The panel shows a font status light and links to the internal install instructions.
- Get written confirmation of Cloud.ru's SB Sans license scope.
- Each item declares its required PostScript names (SBSansDisplay-Regular / -Semibold / -Bold, SBSansText-Regular).
- AE check: app.fonts.getFontsByPostScriptName() + isSubstitute, missingOrSubstitutedFonts and app.project.usedFonts; re-check when fontServerRevision changes.
- Premiere check: Node scan of the Windows/macOS system, per-user and Adobe-only font folders. Match file names first, confirm via the OpenType name table, cache by mtime.
- Warn or block before inserting text templates when a font is missing.

6) DIAGNOSTICS AND VERSIONING
- Logs: one JSONL file per day in %LOCALAPPDATA%\CloudRuBrandKit\logs (mac: ~/Library/Logs/CloudRuBrandKit), rotated at 7 days / 5 MB.
- Each log line records: ts, level, session, plugin version + git sha, host app + version, OS, library version, action, item@version, duration in ms, and error {message, stack, jsx line/file}.
- Every ExtendScript entry point returns {ok, data, error}.
- A 'Copy diagnostics' button copies environment info, the last 200 log lines and the health check.
- Health check covers:
  - host version in the supported range;
  - signature present;
  - fonts;
  - library reachable, its version, cache size and free disk space;
  - the AE 'Allow Scripts to Write Files and Access Network' pref;
  - a version handshake between the panel and its .jsx.
- CEP LogLevel is raised only during support sessions. No external telemetry.
- Plugin: semver, with package.json as the single source feeding manifest.xml ExtensionBundleVersion/Version and a build.json with the git sha.
- Library: calendar versioning with minPluginVersion gating. CHANGELOGs and git tags for both.
- CI: build, sign, verify, then publish the ZXP + sha256 + plugin/latest.json; the panel uses latest.json to show 'update available'.
- A canary machine tests each new AE/Pr release (v27 at MAX) before the team updates.
